Over 16 years have passed since the publication of the Haskell 2010 language report, and the Haskell that we write today has evolved in many ways, some of which are incompatible with the language specified in the Haskell 2010 language report.
In order to account for this change we saw the need to compile a _revised version_ of the Haskell 2010 language report.
The guiding principle of this revision was to not add any new language features, but only to modify the specification of existing language features to take account of how they are implemented (and used) by current Haskell compilers and the wider Haskell ecosystem.

#heading(level: 3, numbering: none)[Changes to the  Report]

The (planned) changes to the report are:
- Functor-Applicative-Monad proposal
- MonadFail proposal
- Monad of no return proposal
- Burning Bridges proposal
- Syntax of numeric literals
- (Unicode) Syntax of identifiers
- Changes to the Num typeclass
- Changes to Bits
- Changes to recursive modules?
- Keyword forall
- "Whitespace around operators" stuff
- etc.
